  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read proxy.retained_record_content and proxy.retained_record_at_the_store. retained_record.rs: RetainedHopRecord::of is now #[cfg(test)] (production builds a record with over(committed.retained(), response) from retained_request, the same builder); covered_set.rs has no diff. durability.rs: the writer, queue and marker-stage code moved into writer_thread.rs, retention_queue.rs and marker_stage.rs; EvidenceRetention::retain became test-only (#[cfg(test)]), so the three cited store tests exercise the writer through the test entry while production goes reserve then complete over the same projection. That is a narrower route to the same record, and this theorem is about what a record holds, not when it is written (THM-0088). The three store tests keep every assertion; they read the archive field instead of archive(). The retention integration test moved to transparency_e2e_test/retention.rs with the same assertions through the Scratch helpers. The claim holds. Every cited Rust test still exists by name; I compared each one's body with its body at the last record's commit and name the ones that differ. Helper functions that unchanged test bodies call were not all diffed. The mutation lane was not run. Evidence class as registered.",
